      "value": "@{62cea1224517083b068f949b|full_name}: The issue lies within Windows 11's Keyboard language \"Microsoft IME Korean/English\" pack, which is the default that most Koreans use.\n\nTo recreate, simply install the Korean Microsoft IME keyboard language pack within Windows settings. Using this keyboard, you can switch input methods between Korean and English using the Right Alt button on your keyboard. You should be able to recreate the problem as I still run into many Korean users who have this issue.\n\nI found the FIX while looking into Windows settings.\n\n1. Settings (Windows)\n\n2. Time & language\n\n3. Language & region\n\n4. Press hamburger menu at the right edge of \"Korean\" and click \"Language Options\"\n\n5. Scroll to bottom and you will see \"Microsoft IME\". Press the hamburger menu at the right edge and click \"Keyboard Options\".\n\n6. Toggle ON for \"Previous version of Microsoft IME\".\n\nThis should fix the issue and you should be able to type without the last letter omitting itself. With that said, I will shed light unto the fact that this issue only arises within VRC, whereas other services and games do not require this fix. Therefore, it is important that we fix this issue so more Korean users using VRC in Windows 11 do not have to share this problem as a whole. Regardless of the outcome in the future, I thank you for your interest and willingness to address this issue.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
