  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "It has been observed that some unprecedented issues emerged with the new VRC update regarding chatboxes, especially when using different language inputs.\n\nAs with my case, the problem arises when I sent my text messages in Korean (exact language input method editor: Microsoft IME Korean). On executing \"send\" after writing my text, the last alphabet is omitted in the chatbox, thus causing confusion and error in the communication process. The users are forced to either a) press spacebar to create a \"null\" alphabet that will be omitted instead of the contents of the message themselves, b) use a punctuation mark at the end, as the punctuation marks do not seems to be omitted when sent, or c) manually click the send button with the mouse instead of pressing enter.\n\nReproduction:\n\n1. Set language to Microsoft IME Korean.\n\n2. Open VRChat.\n\n3. Press Y and type in message\n\n4. Send.\n\nYou will see that the last letter is omitted when sent, and is instead showing up hanging by itself in the chat input ui.",
